{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/13018": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Sport Management",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor, Sport Management Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Assistant Professor, Sport Management Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Assistant Professor, Sport Management Position Status Full-time Tenure Tenure Track Rank Assistant Professor Budget Summary Base Pay $89,288-$93,842 Base Pay $89,288-$93,842 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary Located in the greater Chicago region, Lewis University is a comprehensive Catholic and Lasallian university where the traditions of liberal learning, values, and preparation for professional work come together to create a distinctive educational experience. Founded in 1932, Lewis University offers more than 80 undergraduate majors and programs, 37 graduate programs, and two doctoral programs. The College of Business serves nearly 1,350 students from more than 30 states and 43 countries through eleven undergraduate majors and five graduate programs offered in traditional, online, and accelerated formats. Ethically grounded and career-focused, Lewis business programs combine critical thinking, data analysis, financial understanding, management concepts, and communication skills to prepare graduates for success in today’s global business environment. Our distinguished faculty, comprised of 38 full-time faculty members and more than 75 adjunct instructors, blend academic excellence with extensive professional experience to create an engaging learning environment. The College supports numerous signature initiatives, including the Bryan & Mary Durkin Family Finance & Trading Lab, the Lowell Stahl Center for Entrepreneurship & Real Estate, the Lewis Innovation Hub, the Sales Excellence Program, and dedicated Career Services for Business students. The College of Business invites applications for a full-time, tenure track position in Sport Management at the rank of Assistant Professor. The preferred start date is July 1, 2027. The successful candidate will provide outstanding teaching, professional engagement, scholarship appropriate to AACSB faculty qualification status, student advising, and service to the College, University, and profession. Faculty are expected to support the College’s mission while maintaining professional and/or scholarly currency consistent with AACSB faculty qualification standards. In addition to excellence in teaching, the successful candidate will contribute to the continued growth and visibility of the Sport Management program through curriculum innovation, student mentoring, industry partnerships, and active participation in University service. Please click the link for more information on our benefits Office of Human Resources | Benefit . Responsibilities Essential Duties and Responsibilities: · Teach undergraduate and graduate Sport Management courses in traditional, accelerated, hybrid, and online modalities. · Deliver course instruction aligned with approved student learning outcomes and AACSB standards. · Maintain a twenty-four (24) credit-hour teaching load per academic year. · Develop, revise, and maintain course syllabi, instructional materials, and Blackboard course shells. · Utilize effective instructional practices and technology to enhance student learning and engagement. · Assess student learning, submit grades in accordance with University policy, and participate in program assessment and continuous improvement initiatives. · Maintain regular office hours to advise and mentor students regarding academic success, career planning, internships, and professional development. · Advise undergraduate students regarding degree progression and mentor undergraduate and graduate students on professional development. · Participate actively in curriculum development, accreditation activities, program assessment, student recruitment, retention initiatives, and strategic planning. · Serve on College and University committees and participate in faculty governance. · Establish and maintain collaborative relationships with colleagues, alumni, industry professionals, employers, and community partners. · Demonstrate leadership in establishing, growing, and promoting undergraduate and graduate Sport Management programs. · Maintain academic and/or professional engagement supporting AACSB faculty qualification status through ongoing scholarly activity, professional development, industry engagement, certifications, consulting, or other qualifying activities. · Remain current with emerging trends, issues, and best practices in Sport Management and incorporate those developments into teaching and program initiatives. · Participate in required University and College training, certifications, and professional development. · Perform other duties as assigned by the Department Chair and Dean. Minimum Qualifications AACSB Faculty Qualification Expectations: Faculty members must meet and maintain AACSB qualification as a Scholarly Academic (SA), Practice Academic (PA), Instructional Practitioner (IP), or Scholarly Practitioner (SP) as defined by AACSB standards. Qualification is demonstrated through an appropriate combination of academic preparation, professional experience, scholarly activity, and ongoing academic and/or professional engagement. Faculty are expected to maintain documentation supporting their qualification status throughout their employment. Earned Doctorate in Sport Management, Business Administration, or a closely related discipline from an AACSB -accredited institution. · Minimum of five (5) years (approximately 10,000 hours) of progressively responsible professional experience within the sport management industry. · Ability to teach effectively in face-to-face, hybrid, online, and asynchronous learning environments. · Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, and presentation skills. · Demonstrated ability to build collaborative relationships with faculty, staff, students, and external stakeholders. · Demonstrated commitment to maintaining academic and/or professional engagement consistent with AACSB faculty qualification standards. · Commitment to student success, diversity, equity, inclusion, and working effectively with individuals from diverse backgrounds. Preferred Qualifications - Doctorate in Sport Management, Sport Administration, Business Administration, or a closely related discipline. · Successful university-level teaching experience in Sport Management. · Professional certifications relevant to the discipline. · Established professional network within the sport industry. · Experience developing academic programs, recruiting students, and building industry partnerships. · Experience maintaining AACSB faculty qualification status within an AACSB -accredited College of Business. Essential Duties Work hours Full-time; variable schedule including some evening classes as needed. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00494 Posting Date 10/01/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/12993": {
      "title": "Academic Faculty, MSN Program Director",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Academic Faculty, MSN Program Director Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Academic Faculty, MSN Program Director Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Academic Faculty, MSN Program Director Position Status Full-time Tenure Non-Tenured Rank Assistant Professor Budget Summary Base Pay $85,356-95,685 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary Academic Nursing Faculty in the College of Nursing and Health Sciences to serve in the administrative role of MSN Program Director. The MSN Program Director is the academic leader of the MSN -degree academic program. The Program Director is in charge of managing the day-to-day operation of the program as well as the long-term planning and vision of the program in collaboration and partnership with the Department Chair. Please click the link for more information on our benefits Office of Human Resources | Benefit . Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission and Catholic and Lasallian higher education. -Facilitate student learning through effective teaching and evaluation of learning -Serve as an academic advisor, mentor, and advocate for students in the nursing program The Program Director’s management and leadership responsibilities may include but are not limited to: Leadership • Designs and revises program curriculum with the faculty • Recruits and trains adjunct faculty • Represents the program in College and University matters • Participates in promotion, recruitment, and marketing efforts • Coordinates community partnerships Management • Coordinates advising of students in the program • Coordinates assessment of program Student Learning Outcomes (SLOs), and subsequent action planning • Participates in instructional evaluation of faculty teaching in the program • Serves as an advocate for students and a liaison to centralized services supporting students • Coordinates budgetary issues for the program • Ensures the academic course catalog and website are kept current with updates to program curriculum and/or policies • Coordinates with Admissions for the Graduate Nursing Program Creates the course schedule for the program, including course rotations and faculty assignments • Responds to student concerns and issues -Other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Earned doctoral degree with APRN certification is required. The equivalent of two years of full-time clinical nursing experience. Licensure as a registered professional nurse in the state of Illinois or eligibility with application in process is also required. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated experience in nursing education and/or leadership roles. Essential Duties Work hours TBD Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00492 Posting Date 08/21/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
