    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/12898": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Justice Law and Public Safety Studies",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor, Justice Law and Public Safety Studies Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Assistant Professor, Justice Law and Public Safety Studies Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Assistant Professor, Justice Law and Public Safety Studies Position Status Full-time Tenure Tenure Track Rank Assistant Professor Budget Summary Base Pay 73,560 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary Lewis University’s Department of Justice, Law and Public Safety Studies invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor and Program Director of the undergraduate Criminal Justice and Forensic Criminal Investigation programs. The successful candidate will provide academic leadership for both programs; teach across the undergraduate curriculum; maintain an active research and scholarship agenda; advise and mentor students; and collaborate with faculty and University partners to support curriculum development, assessment, student success, recruitment, and program growth. Teaching assignments may include Research Methods, Introduction to Criminal Justice, Criminology, Introduction to Law Enforcement, Juvenile Justice, Criminalistics, and other courses aligned with the candidate’s expertise and departmental needs. Lewis University serves a diverse student population and community and we invite applications from individuals that embody a commitment to diversity. This position will begin July 2027. Please click the link for more information on our benefits Office of Human Resources | Benefit . Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission and Catholic and Lasallian higher education. Faculty responsibilities include: · Teach 9 credit hours per semester, through a variety of modalities, including face to face, hybrid and online · Academic Advising · Committee assignments · Collaboration with colleagues in ongoing student learning outcomes · General support of departmental initiatives · Active support of the University’s Mission · Availability to maintain a flexible schedule to teach during day and evening hours, attend departmental meetings Program Director responsibilities include: · Designs and revises program curriculum with the faculty · Recruits and trains adjunct faculty · Participates in program recruitment and marketing activities · Represents the program in College and University matters · Participates in promotion, recruitment, and marketing efforts · Coordinates community and organizational partnerships, including community college 3+1 partnership programs · Coordinates advising of students in the program · Coordinates assessment of program Student Learning Outcomes (SLOs), and subsequent action planning · Ensures the academic course catalog is kept current with updates to program curriculum and/or policies · Creates the course schedule for the program, including course rotations and faculty assignments · Responds to student concerns and issues Other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Earned doctorate in Criminal Justice or closely related field or relevant combination of education and professional experience. · 3 years of teaching in higher education · 3 years of experience in a criminal justice-related field · Established research and scholarship agenda · Higher education leadership experience, or leadership experience in a criminal justice-related discipline Preferred Qualifications · 5 years of experience in a criminal justice-related field · Higher education leadership experience · M.S. or M.A. in Forensic Science and/or Forensic Laboratory experience · Record of scholarly publication · Bilingual preferred Essential Duties Work hours Full time faculty position Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00493 Posting Date 10/01/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have bilingual ability in Spanish? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Optional Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
