    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/13069": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Management",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor, Management Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Assistant Professor, Management Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Assistant Professor, Management Position Status Full-time Tenure Tenure Track Rank Assistant Professor Budget Summary Base Pay $89,288 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary Located in the greater Chicago region, Lewis University is a comprehensive, Catholic university, where the traditions of liberal learning, values and preparation for professional work come together to give the university its educational identity and focus. Founded in 1932, Lewis is a dynamic, coeducational university with over 7,000 undergraduate and graduate students. Lewis is one of many schools sponsored by the De LaSalle Christian Brothers, an international Roman Catholic teaching order. Ethically grounded and career-focused, Lewis’ business degree programs combine critical thinking with data analysis, financial understanding, technological knowledge and essential communication skills, preparing students with a well-rounded and comprehensive business foundation. With small class sizes and one-on-one attention from dedicated faculty who are experts in their field, Lewis University’s College of Business programs are accredited by the Accreditation Council for Business Schools and Programs ( ACBSP ). The Lewis University College of Business offers 12 undergraduate majors and serves more than 600 students. Over 500 students are enrolled in the five graduate degree programs, offered through the Graduate School of Management. Please click the link for more information on our benefits: Office of Human Resources | Benefit . Responsibilities The primary professional responsibilities of the Assistant Professor of Management faculty position are to provide outstanding teaching, scholarly research, and service to the Lewis and external communities. Faculty are expected to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, and respectful collaboration and active support for the University’s Mission and for Catholic and Lasallian higher education. The start date for the position is July 1, 2027. Essential Duties: 1. Teach a variety of undergraduate and graduate Management courses, primarily in a face-to-face format on our Romeoville and/or Oak Brook campus. 2. Twenty-Four (24) credit-hour teaching load per contract year. Tenure-Track faculty receive a six (6) credit hour course reduction in their initial year of appointment. 3. Establish and maintain office hours to assist students and foster positive interaction with colleagues and external parties. 5. Advise undergraduate students on program progression and academic success. Additionally, mentor graduate and undergraduate students on professional development. 6. Actively participate in College/University Committees, scholarly pursuits, student recruitment, recognition events and other various duties as assigned by the Dean and Department Chair. 7. Participate in curriculum development and program assessment. 8. Actively network with current business professionals, incorporating current topics and trends within the classroom. 9. Maintain academic and/or professional engagement supporting AACSB faculty qualification status through ongoing scholarly activity, professional development, industry engagement, certifications, consulting, or other qualifying activities. AACSB Faculty Qualification Expectations Faculty members must meet and maintain AACSB qualification as a Scholarly Academic (SA), Practice Academic (PA), Instructional Practitioner (IP), or Scholarly Practitioner (SP) as defined by AACSB standards. Qualification is demonstrated through an appropriate combination of academic preparation, professional experience, scholarly activity, and ongoing academic and/or professional engagement. Faculty are expected to maintain documentation supporting their qualification status throughout their employment. Minimum Qualifications 1. Earned doctorate in Management, or other related business discipline from an AACSB -accredited institution. Strong candidates who are ABD and nearing completion of their dissertations at AACSB -accredited institutions will be considered. 2. Experience with course development and evidence of successful teaching ability at the university level. 3. Demonstrated ability to establish productive and collaborative working relationships with other faculty and staff. 4. Experience supporting student development and professional growth beyond the classroom. 5. Active engagement in research and professional development interests. 6. Experience tailoring instruction to support diverse learning needs in an academic setting. 7. Demonstrated commitment to maintaining academic and/or professional engagement consistent with AACSB faculty qualification standards. Preferred Qualifications 1. Experience teaching Management courses at the university level from an AACSB -accredited institution. 2. Experience in a leadership role in a corporate/business environment. 3. Established industry and professional network. 4. Demonstrated ability to publish high-quality research in peer-reviewed publications. 5. Experience maintaining AACSB faculty qualification status within an AACSB -accredited College of Business. Essential Duties Work hours Full-time Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00498 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H-1B status)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/13073": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Justice, Law and Public Safety Studies",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty, Justice, Law and Public Safety Studies Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Adjunct Faculty, Justice, Law and Public Safety Studies Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Justice, Law and Public Safety Studies Position Status Adjunct Tenure Non-Tenured Rank Lecturer Budget Summary Base Pay Adjunct Salary Position Summary Information Job Description Summary The Department of Justice, Law and Public Safety Studies is requesting applications for instructors to teach in the undergraduate Criminal Justice Program. Responsibilities -Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission and Catholic and Lasallian higher education. -Teach courses for the Department of Justice, Law & Public Safety programs, including Research Methods and foundational courses in the Criminal Justice major. -Applicants must be available to teach on campus in Romeoville, IL and/or at partner community colleges within a 25-mile radius of Lewis University, beginning January, 2027. Minimum Qualifications The applicants seeking to teach in the Criminal Justice program must possess a minimum of a Master’s degree in Criminal Justice, Science, or closely related field. Extensive experience, background and expertise in any of the Justice, Law & Public Safety disciplines may be applicable. Preferred Qualifications Essential Duties Work hours Part-time; as needed basis. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00321 Posting Date 11/10/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Lewis provides course sections taught in English and in Spanish. If a Spanish section is available within your discipline, are you comfortable teaching in Spanish? This question will NOT negatively impact consideration of your application for employment, and your participation is voluntary. Yes/No Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Transcripts Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
